{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21934 - PROTEIN:5028",
  "verbalization": "Nervisterol is implicated in the biological activity of COLO-824 through a series of molecular interactions involving macrophage scavenger receptor types I and II. These receptors are targets of both Lupinine and (-)-Dicentrine, which in turn are targets of Nervisterol. This suggests a hierarchical pathway where Nervisterol influences the activity of these receptors, which then modulate the behavior of COLO-824. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a robust mechanism where Nervisterol acts as a regulator of macrophage scavenger receptors, which are key in cellular processes that may affect COLO-824. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Nervisterol in influencing the cellular environment of COLO-824, though the exact nature of this influence remains to be fully elucidated.",
